> Exact search with a separator that cannot be a byte

For pattern \(P\) of length \(m\) and text \(T\) of length \(n\),
consider the virtual sequence

$$
S=P\;\Vert\;\langle256\rangle\;\Vert\;T.
$$
\alttext(The virtual sequence consists of the pattern, the integer sentinel 256 and the text.)

Every input byte is interpreted as an unsigned value from 0 to 255, so the
sentinel cannot equal any input symbol. For an index \(i\ge m+1\) in
the text region, \(Z_S[i]=m\) exactly when a complete pattern begins
at text offset \(i-m-1\). The sentinel prevents an extension beyond
\(m\). All overlaps are retained.

The library accesses this conceptual sequence without copying a joined
string. It stores the Z-array, giving \(O(n+m)\) time and temporary
storage for one fitting nonempty pattern. Unlike the old fixed-byte
separator contract, no input byte is reserved. Empty patterns keep the
existing API convention of matching every boundary \(0,\ldots,n\),
with no preprocessing; a pattern longer than the text also returns early.

> Applying it to every passenger name

Each name is searched as a separate record. In particular, a query cannot
match the end of one surname followed by the beginning of another record.
The work size includes each record's virtual pattern and sentinel when
preprocessing runs. A sum of per-record linear bounds provides a direct
check of the implementation's guarantee.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/z_algorithm_names.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
  const auto work = dm::algorithms::z_search_summary(dm::datasets::titanic(), "Name",
      {"Mr.", "Mrs.", "Miss.", "Master.", "William", "Anna"});
  std::print("{}\n", work.to_md());
  std::vector<double> x(work.nrows());
  std::iota(x.begin(), x.end(), 0);
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
  dm::graphics::RPlot::create()
      .bars(x, work.get_column("comparisons").values(), "actual comparisons", dm::RGB{147, 197, 253})
      .points(x, work.get_column("comparison_bound").values(), "sum of linear bounds", dm::RGB{220, 38, 38}, 5)
      .x_ticks(x, work.get_column<std::string>("pattern").values())
      .title("Actual Z-search work on 891 separate passenger names")
      .x_label("query").y_label("symbol equality tests").size(1000, 480).save_svg("build/z_algorithm_names.svg");
}
```
